\section{Gravitational decoherence.}
The fundamental problem in quantum gravity is this: if a single massive object is prepared in a superposition of two different locations with respect to a fixed coordinate frame, the resulting gravitational field must be non stationary.  An example is shown in Fig. (\ref{cat-mass-clock}).
\begin{figure}[h]
